  <h3 class="accordion__header is-closed">
<button type="button"
          class="accordion__title is-collapsed aalto-anchor-link-heading aalto-anchor-link-skip-toc"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls="accordion-content--5"
          id="accordion-title--5"><span class="accordion__title-text">

                    Thesis
            </span></button></h3>
<div class="accordion__content is-collapsed" aria-labelledby="accordion-title--5" id="accordion-content--5">
  
                    <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><p>JOIN.bsc Bachelor's Thesis and Seminar is a 10 ECTS study module that is completed during one study term in third year of studies. The bachelor’s thesis is written while attending the seminar.</p>
<p>After completing the Bachelor’s Thesis and Seminar you will be able to understand scientific processes and search for relevant background information, both applying and analysing the data collected. In addition, you will be able to produce scientific articles in precise and correct language, present your findings and both receive and give feedback.</p>
<p>The language of instruction of the seminar is English and the thesis is written in English. Students who have been educated in Finnish or Swedish are required to write their maturity essay in the language of education (i.e. Finnish or Swedish).</p>
<p>More information on the Bachelor's Thesis and Seminar will be provided to students during their studies in the programme.</p></div>
            
  </div>

  <h3 class="accordion__header is-closed">
<button type="button"
          class="accordion__title is-collapsed aalto-anchor-link-heading aalto-anchor-link-skip-toc"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls="accordion-content--6"
          id="accordion-title--6"><span class="accordion__title-text">

                    Minor 20–25 ECTS
            </span></button></h3>
<div class="accordion__content is-collapsed" aria-labelledby="accordion-title--6" id="accordion-content--6">
  
                    <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><p>A minor subject of 20–25 ECTS is a compulsory part of a bachelor's degree. The combined extent of the minor (20–25 ECTS) and the elective studies in Chemical Engineering (19-24 ECTS) is 44 ECTS. The minor is confirmed in the student’s personal study plan (HOPS). It is possible to <a href="/en/minors#/">choose a minor within Aalto University</a> or from university abroad during a student exchange.</p>
<p>Minor studies must be university level subject studies and they must form a module. It is not possible to take individual courses or language courses as a minor. Also studies in the field of student's major and courses that overlap with other studies are excluded from the minor selection.</p>
<h3>Minor from Aalto University</h3>
<p>Minor subjects offered by the different disciplines at Aalto University are listed on <a href="/en/minors#/">Minors</a>. The minor modules of Aalto University Language Centre are not suitable as actual minors.</p>
<p>Currently, minors that are offered in English and are suitable for bachelor's level students include at least the following:</p>
<ul>
<li>Bioinformation Technology (School of ELEC)</li>
<li>Collaborative Product Development (School of ENG)</li>
<li>Computer Engineering (School of ELEC)</li>
<li>Computational Engineering&nbsp;(School of ENG)</li>
<li>Computer Science&nbsp;Y (School of SCI)</li>
<li>Computer Science&nbsp;L (School of SCI)</li>
<li>Data Science&nbsp;(School of SCI)</li>
<li>Digital Systems and Design&nbsp;(School of ELEC)</li>
<li>Economics&nbsp;(School of BIZ)</li>
<li>Finance (School of BIZ)</li>
<li>Information and Service Management&nbsp;(School of BIZ)</li>
<li>Information Technology Programme&nbsp;(School of BIZ)</li>
<li>International Business&nbsp;(School of BIZ)</li>
<li>Mathematics&nbsp;(School of SCI)</li>
<li>Quantitative Methods&nbsp;(School of BIZ)</li>
<li>Quantum Technology&nbsp;(Schools of ELEC and SCI)</li>
<li>Statistics&nbsp;(School of SCI)</li>
</ul></div>
            
  </div>

  <h3 class="accordion__header is-closed">
<button type="button"
          class="accordion__title is-collapsed aalto-anchor-link-heading aalto-anchor-link-skip-toc"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls="accordion-content--7"
          id="accordion-title--7"><span class="accordion__title-text">

                    Elective Studies 19–24 ECTS
            </span></button></h3>
<div class="accordion__content is-collapsed" aria-labelledby="accordion-title--7" id="accordion-content--7">
  
                    <div class="aalto-user-generated-content"><p>Chemical Engineering major students choose 19-24 ECTS of elective studies. The combined extent of the minor and the elective studies is 44 ECTS.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Individual elective courses can be taken from other programmes at Aalto University, other Finnish universities through possible RIPA agreements or studies completed abroad during a student exchange. Exchange studies can also form an international minor or be included in the major. You can also select courses in the&nbsp;<a href="https://www.unite-university.eu/learn/student-catalogue?sfr">European Unite! universities</a>.</p>
<p>You can also choose an elective minor. The Language Centre's minor subjects are always placed in elective studies.</p>
<p>If you plan to continue to one of the master’s programmes at the School of Chemical Engineering, you should select from the courses listed below.</p>
<p><strong>Biotechnology</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>CHEM-C2300 Cell and Molecular Biology</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Chemical and Metallurgical Engineering</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>CHEM-C2150 Process Design</li>
<li>CHEM-A1120 Fluid Flow and Heat Transfer</li>
<li>CHEM-C2160 Unit Operations</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Chemistry and Materials Science</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>CHEM-C3410 Nanomaterials</li>
<li>CHEM-C2245 Inorganic Chemistry Book Exam</li>
<li>CHEM-A1290 Fundamentals of Organic Chemistry</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Bioproducts Engineering</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>No extra courses required</li>
</ul>
<p>Elective studies must be university level studies that fulfill the degree requirements and, in general, studies that are offered as degree studies at the university in question.&nbsp;</p>
<p>The elective studies may include a work placement furthering professional development. It is possible to include 1–10 ECTS of work experience in a bachelor’s degree. Work experience can be included easily as the study unit JOIN.trai Practical training.</p>
<p>Entrepreneurial, multidisciplinary Aalto studies and language and communication courses offered by Aalto University Language Centre are recommended as elective studies.&nbsp;Foreign students are encouraged to take Finnish courses.</p></div>
            
  </div>

</div>
      </div>
  </div>

      </div>

      
  <div class="aalto-component-wrapper aalto-component  aalto-component-wrapper--text-accordion"
